  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "V: View",
      "items": [
        "The screen: labels, buttons, lists, forms",
        "Passive: it renders exactly what the Presenter hands it",
        "Reports taps and typing as events, e.g. 'Save tapped'",
        "Holds no state it could not redraw from the view model",
        "Easy to swap or test with a fake Presenter",
        "Example: Accounts View lists accounts and reports 'Add tapped'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "I: Interactor",
      "items": [
        "One use case per method, e.g. 'add a transaction'",
        "Applies business rules: validation, totals, balances",
        "Reads and saves data through Entities and storage",
        "Returns plain results, never display text",
        "No UI imports, so it tests without a screen",
        "Example: Transactions Interactor checks an entry then saves a Transaction"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "P: Presenter",
      "items": [
        "The coordinator for one screen",
        "Receives View events and decides which use case to call",
        "Formats results: dates, currency, empty states, errors",
        "Pushes a ready-to-draw view model to the View",
        "Asks the Router to move on, never builds screens itself",
        "Example: Budgets Presenter turns 4500 cents into '$45.00 of $60.00 used'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "E: Entity",
      "items": [
        "The core domain objects, e.g. Account, Transaction, Money",
        "Plain data with simple invariants, no persistence code",
        "Passed between Interactors and storage",
        "Know nothing about screens, flows or the Presenter",
        "Stay stable while the UI changes around them",
        "Examples: Account, Transaction and Category are separate Entities that any module's Interactor can share"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "R: Router",
      "items": [
        "Also called the Wireframe: owns how screens connect",
        "Creates the next module's View, Presenter and Interactor and wires them",
        "Handles presenting, pushing and dismissing screens",
        "Passes any data the next module needs",
        "Keeps modules decoupled: only the Router knows its neighbours",
        "Example: Accounts Router builds the Transactions module when an account is opened"
      ]
    }
  ]
}